@flexiarg snatch/accept-an-offer-that-beats-holding
@title Accept an Offer That Beats Holding
@audience responding players
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/exchange-when-both-sides-gain
@see-also snatch/revert-then-invert

! conclusion: As P2, accept a balanced offer whose exchange payoff beats keeping the tokens asked of you.

  + context: **Play grain.** P2 has received a positive give/ask offer and must
    accept, refuse, or snatch.

  + IF:
    The offered tokens are worth more to you than the asked tokens you would
    retain, and the offer leaves P1 a positive exchange gain too.

  + HOWEVER:
    Snatching dominates acceptance only when future marks, denunciation, and
    continued mutually beneficial exchanges are priced at zero; refusal throws
    away the current surplus outright.

  + THEN:
    Accept, treating offer size as both a current payoff and evidence of how much
    cooperative exchange the proposer is prepared to sustain.

  + BECAUSE:
    Acceptance captures positive value now while preserving the counterpart and
    the repeated exchange. Under G4, the possible inverse transfer makes seizure
    still less attractive.
